### Task 4: User-space prep ×9 (user.ld, build.rs, cfg flip, brand!) — inert on the old target

All four edits repeat across the 9 crates. They are deliberately inert while the nested builds still target `aarch64-unknown-none` (cfg gates false, note section empty), so this commit still boots. **Contingency:** if lld errors on the declared-but-empty `note` PT_NOTE phdr at link time, fold this task's commit into Task 5's (single commit); do not restructure otherwise.

**Files (pattern ×9; representative: `servers/pm/`):**
- Modify: `<crate>/user.ld` (two hunks — the files differ only in leading comments; apply hunks per-file, do NOT wholesale-replace)
- Create: `<crate>/build.rs`
- Modify: `<crate>/src/main.rs` (cfg flip + brand call)
- Modify: `<crate>/Cargo.toml` (abi-note dep + lints inheritance)

- [ ] **Step 1: user.ld hunk A** — PHDRS gains the note phdr:

```ld
PHDRS {
    text   PT_LOAD FLAGS(5); /* R+X */
    rodata PT_LOAD FLAGS(4); /* R   */
    data   PT_LOAD FLAGS(6); /* RW  */
    note   PT_NOTE FLAGS(4); /* minixrs identity note */
}
```

- [ ] **Step 2: user.ld hunk B** — replace the `.rodata` region (current lines 36–39 in `servers/pm/user.ld`):

```ld
    . = ALIGN(4K);
    /*
     * minixrs identity note (tooling/docs/abi-note.md): first thing in the
     * RO segment, dual-assigned so it lands in the rodata PT_LOAD *and* its
     * own PT_NOTE phdr. KEEP() is mandatory — nothing references the
     * section — and this rule must stay ahead of the /DISCARD/ *(.note.*)
     * rule below (first match wins).
     */
    .note.minixrs.ident : {
        KEEP(*(.note.minixrs.ident))
    } :rodata :note

    .rodata : {
        *(.rodata .rodata.*)
    } :rodata
```

(The RO PT_LOAD now *starts* with the 28-byte note at a page-aligned vaddr/offset; `.rodata` follows in the same segment — hence dropping its own `ALIGN(4K)`. The `/DISCARD/` rule keeps its `*(.note .note.*)` line; it now only eats foreign notes because first-match wins.)

- [ ] **Step 3: per-crate `build.rs`** (SPDX header + exactly this, per minixrs-m1.md Step 4 — the cfg gate keeps host clippy/check linker-flag-free):

```rust
fn main() {
    println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed=user.ld");
    if std::env::var("CARGO_CFG_TARGET_OS").as_deref() == Ok("minixrs") {
        let dir = std::env::var("CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR").unwrap();
        println!("cargo:rustc-link-arg=-T{dir}/user.ld");
    }
}
```

- [ ] **Step 4: cfg flip in main.rs** — change each `_start` gate from
`#[cfg_attr(target_os = "none", unsafe(link_section = ".text._start"))]` to
`#[cfg_attr(target_os = "minixrs", unsafe(link_section = ".text._start"))]`
(sites: pm:107, vfs:112, ds:45, sched:55, rs:69, vm:72, tty:73, init:37, worker:37 — vm's lacks the `#[cfg(not(test))]`/`#[unsafe(no_mangle)]` neighbors, that's pre-existing, leave it). Update the adjacent comment ("gated to the bare-metal target" → "gated to the minixrs target"). These are the ONLY 9 `target_os` occurrences outside `kernel/` (verified by grep — `server-rt`/`minix-ipc`/`driver-rt` have none; kernel-side `"none"` cfgs stay).

- [ ] **Step 5: brand the binary** — after the crate attrs in each `main.rs`:

```rust
minixrs_abi_note::brand!();
```

and in each Cargo.toml `[dependencies]`: `minixrs-abi-note = { path = "../../minixrs-abi-note" }`, plus add to each of the 9:

```toml
[lints]
workspace = true
```

- [ ] **Step 6: Gates + boot** — `cargo fmt --all`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`; then `timeout 25 cargo run -p minixrs-kernel --target aarch64-unknown-none --release > <scratchpad>/boot-task4.log 2>&1`; `tools/check-boot-log.sh <scratchpad>/boot-task4.log` — clean (everything inert: cfg false on the old target, so no note, no link-arg from the new build.rs; kernel/build.rs still injects `-T` via CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS).
