### Task 5: Target JSON + kernel/build.rs switch + pack-time brand assertion

**Files:**
- Create: `tools/targets/aarch64-unknown-minixrs.json`
- Modify: `kernel/build.rs` (`build_boot_image` ~lines 106–166, `build_server` ~lines 168–231)
- Modify: `kernel/Cargo.toml` (`[build-dependencies]`)

- [ ] **Step 1: Create the JSON** — copy **verbatim from minixrs-m1.md Step 1** (verified this session: it is byte-for-byte the pinned nightly's `aarch64-unknown-none` spec output minus `metadata`, plus `"os": "minixrs"`; `llvm-target` stays `aarch64-unknown-none`). On future nightly bumps: regenerate with `rustc -Zunstable-options --print target-spec-json --target aarch64-unknown-none` and re-apply the one `"os"` line.

- [ ] **Step 2: Rework `build_server`** — new body (signature loses the now-unused `out_dir` param):

```rust
fn build_server(
    crate_name: &str,
    crate_dir: &std::path::Path,
    workspace: &std::path::Path,
    extra_args: &[&str],
) -> PathBuf {
    // One shared nested target dir (not per-crate): -Zbuild-std would otherwise
    // rebuild core+alloc 9x per kernel build. Nested invocations run
    // sequentially from this script; cargo's own locking covers any overlap
    // with developer commands. Still separate from the outer `target/` root,
    // so nesting cargo here cannot deadlock on the kernel build's lock.
    let target_dir = workspace.join("target/minixrs-user");
    let target_json = workspace.join("tools/targets/aarch64-unknown-minixrs.json");

    for path in [
        crate_dir.join("src"),
        crate_dir.join("user.ld"),
        crate_dir.join("Cargo.toml"),
    ] {
        println!("cargo:rerun-if-changed={}", path.display());
    }

    let cargo = std::env::var("CARGO").unwrap_or_else(|_| "cargo".into());
    let status = Command::new(cargo)
        .current_dir(workspace)
        .args(["build", "-p", crate_name, "--target"])
        .arg(&target_json)
        .args([
            "--release",
            // Custom target ⇒ no prebuilt core/alloc; `compiler-builtins-mem`
            // provides memcpy/memset (harmless if a future nightly defaults it).
            "-Zbuild-std=core,alloc",
            "-Zbuild-std-features=compiler-builtins-mem",
        ])
        .args(extra_args)
        .env("CARGO_TARGET_DIR", &target_dir)
        // The servers' -T<user.ld> now comes from each crate's own build.rs
        // (cfg-gated on target_os = "minixrs"); scrub any inherited rustflags
        // so the kernel's -Tlinker.ld (or a user's env) can't leak in.
        .env_remove("RUSTFLAGS")
        .env_remove("CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS")
        .status()
        .unwrap_or_else(|e| panic!("failed to spawn cargo for {crate_name}: {e}"));
    if !status.success() {
        panic!("building {crate_name} (server ELF) failed");
    }

    let elf = target_dir.join(format!("aarch64-unknown-minixrs/release/{crate_name}"));
    assert!(elf.exists(), "{crate_name} ELF missing at {}", elf.display());
    elf
}
```

Rewrite the function's doc comment (the old one documents the CARGO_ENCODED_RUSTFLAGS cancel-hack and per-crate isolation dirs — both gone). Update the call site in `build_boot_image` (drop the `out_dir` argument).

- [ ] **Step 3: Extend the shared watch list** in `build_boot_image` (lines 115–121) with the two new inputs:

```rust
        workspace.join("minixrs-abi-note/src"),
        workspace.join("tools/targets/aarch64-unknown-minixrs.json"),
```

- [ ] **Step 4: Pack-time brand assertion** — `kernel/Cargo.toml`:

```toml
[build-dependencies]
cc = "1"
minixrs-kernel-shared = { path = "../kernel-shared" }
```

and in `build_boot_image`'s loop, right after `let bytes = std::fs::read(&elf)…` (line ~156):

```rust
        // Pack-time gate: refuse to embed an unbranded/foreign ELF. Runtime
        // enforcement in load_exec_image stays authoritative — exec-from-FS
        // (slice 5.9) bypasses this assertion entirely.
        if let Err(e) = minixrs_kernel_shared::brand::scan_brand(&bytes) {
            panic!("{}: missing/bad minixrs brand: {e:?}", elf.display());
        }
```

- [ ] **Step 5: Build + boot + inspect.** `timeout 25 cargo run -p minixrs-kernel --target aarch64-unknown-none --release > <scratchpad>/boot-task5.log 2>&1` then `tools/check-boot-log.sh <scratchpad>/boot-task5.log` — clean. Also boot `--no-default-features` once (PM's `--no-default-features` extra arg must still thread through).

- [ ] **Step 6: Verify the ELFs** (paths now `target/minixrs-user/aarch64-unknown-minixrs/release/minixrs-{vm,ds,tty,vfs,sched,rs,pm,init,worker}`):

```bash
ELFS=$(printf 'target/minixrs-user/aarch64-unknown-minixrs/release/minixrs-%s ' vm ds tty vfs sched rs pm init worker)
~/src/tooling/verify/check-brand.sh $ELFS   # exit 0, each line "BRANDED minixrs abi_version=1 flags=0"
# Program headers: exactly 3 page-aligned PT_LOAD + 1 PT_NOTE per ELF.
READELF=$(find "$(rustc --print sysroot)" -name 'llvm-readelf' | head -1)
[ -n "$READELF" ] || READELF="$(find "$(rustc --print sysroot)" -name 'llvm-readobj' | head -1) --elf-output-style=GNU"
for f in $ELFS; do $READELF -lW "$f"; done
```

